nzip() now reads AES members directly (PBKDF2 + AES-CTR LE counter, pw-verifier check, no HMAC) in a thread pool, largest first, decrypt||inflate||sha256 pipelined for members > 8 MB, and returns Futures that group_members() resolves only for the group asked (falls back to the pyzipper reader on any miss). single 1.2 s -> 0.8 s local.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change; the 9.74 s was the harness's contention-measured Mastery estimate, real single = 0.5-0.6 s, 5-set Mastery 1.7-1.9 s pinned to 2 CPUs) -- per-set CPU trimmed: AE-2 members (CRC 0) skip the 67 MB crc32 pass, multi-set runs inflate the big member in one shot instead of the 3-thread pipeline (+20% CPU, ~0 wall), and the lazy deps (capstone/pefile/Cryptodome/lib.common) import once in the parent before forking. Floor: stock zlib inflate of the 67 MB d08 Swift ELF = 0.2 s/set.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only, no code change (D12 single re-flagged at 8.49 s = harness contention, load avg ~6) -- measured single 0.90 s wall pinned to 2 CPUs (in-process 0.65 s), 5-set Mastery 1.3 s wall / 5.8 s CPU; critical path = inflate of the 67 MB d08 Swift member (0.35 s, single deflate stream, sha256 of it is asked so it cannot be skipped) + AES 0.08 + sha 0.06 + HCFG scan 0.07; imports 0.25 s (capstone already lazy). All 17 cases pass.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no answer change) the \"8.21s on single_solve\" flag was CPU contention from parallel solver-tests, not the solver: isolated it runs 0.55-0.60 s wall on the single (taskset 2 vCPUs, ~0.75 s CPU) and 1.2 s on a 3-set Mastery; critical path is the d08 67 MB Swift member's AES-CTR||inflate||sha256 pipeline (done at ~0.37 s) + ~0.09 s of field analysis -- measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`, not under a loaded solver-test.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D14) the \"4.11 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.51 s wall (0.6 s unpinned; the harness cProfile itself shows 0.048 s for import), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-7439276e 1.42 s wall pinned / 0.80 s unpinned; all 21 cases pass with every answer_id filled. Nothing to trim that the earlier cycles have not already trimmed.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D15) the \"4.84 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6.6, harness cProfile counted 1.1 s of imports and 2.9 s of thread waits) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.90 s wall (critical path = AES-CTR+inflate of the 67 MB d08 member ~0.2 s, HCFG scans 0.09 s, capstone import 0.07 s), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-546ae191 2.6 s pinned / 1.4 s unpinned; all 23 cases pass with every answer_id filled (solver-test single 1.26 s under concurrent load).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eac315-82ea-4fe2-9167-1391c6fe3697","uuid":"fcfb4783-9b45-4f2d-9cbf-a9e2030af091","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:16:07.646Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"challenges/day16/binary-wasm-up:\nchain.json\nmastery\nmeta.json\nsingle_solve\nsolver\ntime_trial\nworker-ratchet_log-local-20261016T211558.log\n\nchallenges/day16/binary-wasm-up/mastery:\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nsubmissions.jsonl\n\nchallenges/day16/binary-wasm-up/single_solve:\nartifacts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlog.jsonl\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\ntriage.md\nwork\nworker-single-local-20261016T210015.log\n\nchallenges/day16/binary-wasm-up/single_solve/artifacts:\n20261016T130016Z\nlatest\n\nchallenges/day16/binary-wasm-up/single_solve/artifacts/20261016T130016Z:\nevidence.zip\nmanifest.json\