{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018eZwMdcUB6rS2PRA8dCyfT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D15, 2026-10-15)\n2\t\n3\tScope: what a D16+ `evidence.zip` group could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\n4\tare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D15), `challenges/day15/binary-stripped/solver/NOTES.md`,\n5\t`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n6\t`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n7\t\n8\tProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\n9\tlanguage); D15 = first non-language TWIST (stripped + symbolized pair, new `<qualifier>_` id prefix). Asked field names are a small\n10\tfixed pool (config_*, format, machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names,\n11\tdisassembly, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, xor_key_hex, metadata_version,\n12\tcompression_methods); the prompt's language theme has not been asked since D4. So for D16+ the biggest risks are (a) a twist that\n13\thides the HCFG from a byte scan (packing, real crypto, stack-built), (b) a new container/arch whose LABEL we have never spelled\n14\t(Mach-O, WASM, AArch64, MIPS...), (c) a new field family (imports, build-id, protections).\n15\t\n16\tTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n17\tInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\n18\tllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\n19\trizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\n20\tAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\n21\tjadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara,\n22\t7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\n23\tlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\n24\tMissing: qemu-user(-static), wabt (wasm2wat/wasm-objdump), FLOSS, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\n25\tunluac/luajit-decompiler, blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n26\t\n27\t## Concept table\n28\t\n29\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D16+ likelihood |\n30\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n31\t| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] `readelf -hSW f; readelf -sW f; objdump -d -M intel f` | high (carry-over every day; mastery d01 re-rolls stripped/renamed) |\n32\t| 2 | C++ Itanium ELF / MinGW PE32+ | seen D2 | `_Z` symbols, `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`, `libstdc++`; PE `.text$_Z...` COMDAT, `.CRT`, `.tls` | [I] `nm -C f`; `objdump -t f.exe`; `c++filt` | high (carry-over; ELF/PE re-rolls per member) |\n33\t| 3 | .NET C# PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over) |\n34\t| 4 | Go (static, stripped; PE in Mastery) | seen D4 | `\\xff Go buildinf:`, `.gopclntab`, `runtime.`, `go1.NN` | [I] `GoReSym -t -d -p f`; `go version -m f`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` | high (carry-over) |\n35\t| 5 | Rust ELF (debug_info) | seen D5 | `_ZN...17h<16hex>E` / `_R` v0 symbols, `rustc version`, `/rustc/<sha>/library` panic paths | [I] `rustfilt < syms`; `readelf -p .comment f` | high (carry-over) |\n36\t| 6 | Rust stripped / release | gap | no `.symtab`, panic strings + `/rustc/<40hex>/` paths remain, `core::fmt` strings | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m3 /rustc/`; Ghidra headless; [M] no cargo-rustc symbol-recovery tool | med (natural \"stripped\" sequel for any language) |\n37\t| 7 | Java / Kotlin jar | seen D6, D7 | `PK` + `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`, `CAFEBABE` classes, `kotlin/` packages | [I] `unzip -l f.jar; javap -v -p -c Main.class`; `jadx -d out f.jar`; `lib.binary.jar_app_classes` | high (carry-over) |\n38\t| 8 | Swift ELF (static stdlib, 67 MB) | seen D8 | `swift5_*` sections, `$s` symbols, `libswiftCore` | [I] `bin/swift-demangle`; regex `SENGR` in `.rodata` | high (carry-over) |\n39\t| 9 | Nim / D / Crystal ELF | seen D9, D11, D13 | Nim `NimMain`,`fatal.nim`; D `_D4core`,`DMDH`; Crystal `Crystal:H`,`GC_malloc` | [I] `bin/nim-demangle`; `grep -abo 'SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/=]*' f` | high (carry-over) |\n40\t| 10 | Zig ELF + PE | seen D10 | `.comment` \"zig-bootstrap\"/LLD 19, stripped, `.hcfg` section | [I] `readelf -p .comment f; readelf -x .hcfg f` | high (carry-over) |\n41\t| 11 | Free Pascal ELF | seen D12 | `FPC 3.2.2`, `.fpcdata`, `FPC_` symbols, static stripped | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep FPC`; `grep -abo HCFG f` | high (carry-over) |\n42\t| 12 | Objective-C (GNUstep) ELF | seen D14 | `__objc_selectors`/`__objc_classes`, `objc_msg_lookup`, `._OBJC_CLASS_` | [I] `readelf -sW f \\| grep -E '_OBJC_CLASS_\\|objc_sel_name_'` | high (carry-over) |\n43\t| 13 | Haskell (GHC) | gap | `hs_main`, `ghczmprim_`/`base_GHCziBase` z-encoded symbols, `GHC <ver>` rts strings, huge static ELF | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m2 'GHC '`; `nm f \\| grep -c _info$`; [M] no hsdecomp | med (classic \"weird runtime\" language left on the list) |\n44\t| 14 | OCaml native | gap | `caml_startup`, `camlStdlib__`, `caml_main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM` | [I] `nm f \\| grep -m5 '^.* T caml'`; `strings -a f \\| grep -i ocaml` | med |\n45\t| 15 | V language | gap | `main__main`, `v__`/`builtin__` symbols, compiled via C (`.comment` GCC/tcc) | [I] `nm f \\| grep -E 'main__main\\|builtin__'` | low-med |\n46\t| 16 | Dart AOT (`dart compile exe`) / Flutter `libapp.so` | gap | `_kDartVmSnapshotData`/`_kDartIsolateSnapshotInstructions` symbols, `Dart_` strings, snapshot hash | [I] `readelf -sW f \\| grep _kDart`; [M] blutter (`github.com/worawit/blutter`) | low-med (snapshot strings are compressed: HCFG may not be byte-visible) |\n47\t| 17 | Fortran (gfortran) | gap | `_gfortran_` imports, `MAIN__`, `libgfortran.so.5` NEEDED | [I] `readelf -dW f \\| grep NEEDED`; `nm -D f \\| grep gfortran` | med (pun-friendly title, trivial for organizers) |\n48\t| 18 | Ada (GNAT) | gap | `__gnat_`, `ada_main`, `GNAT Version: N`, `libgnat` | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m1 'GNAT Version'` | med |\n49\t| 19 | Erlang/Elixir BEAM | gap | `FOR1....BEAM` IFF chunks (`AtU8`,`Code`,`LitT` zlib), escript `#!` + zip | [M] `erl -noshell -eval 'beam_lib:chunks(...)'` (apt erlang-base); [I] python `zlib` on `LitT` | low-med (would be a new container: format label unknown) |\n50\t| 20 | Heavy AOT runtimes: Julia, GraalVM native-image, Kotlin/Native | gap | Julia `libjulia`, `jl_`; GraalVM `__svm_`, `com.oracle.svm`; K/N `kfun:`, `Konan_` | [I] `nm f \\| grep -m5 -E 'kfun:\\|__svm\\|jl_'`; `strings -a f` | low-med (K/N most likely: Kotlin already a theme) |\n51\t| 21 | Python frozen: PyInstaller / Nuitka / py2exe | gap (tooled) | PyInstaller cookie `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `pydata` section, `_MEIPASS`; Nuitka `__nuitka`, `NUITKA_ONEFILE`; py2exe `PYTHONSCRIPT` resource | [I] `bin/pyinstxtractor f; bin/pycdc x.pyc`; Nuitka: `strings -a f` + constants blob; [I] `uncompyle6`/`decompyle3` | med (blurs into script lane; HCFG would sit in a marshalled const) |\n52\t| 22 | Lua / LuaJIT bytecode | gap | `\\x1bLua` + version 0x51-0x54; `\\x1bLJ` (LuaJIT); embedded in a C host | [I] `xxd -l 16 f`; [M] `luac -l -l` (apt lua5.4), unluac jar, luajit-decompiler-v2 | low-med |\n53\t| 23 | Legacy Windows: Delphi, VB6, AutoIt | gap (AutoIt tooled) | Delphi `Borland`/`Embarcadero`, `DVCLAL`, `PACKAGEINFO` RCDATA; VB6 `MSVBVM60.DLL`, `VB5!`; AutoIt `AU3!EA06`, RCDATA `SCRIPT` | [I] `bin/autoit-ripper f.exe out/`; python `pefile` resources; [M] IDR/DIE | low (lane is Linux-first; Pascal already done via FPC) |\n54\t| 24 | Niche native langs: Odin, Hare, Vala, GnuCOBOL, Chapel | gap | Odin `runtime.`/`__$startup_runtime`; Vala `g_object_`/GLib; COBOL `cob_init`, `libcob` | [I] `readelf -dW f \\| grep NEEDED`; `nm f \\| head` | med (the organizers clearly have a \"one more language\" list) |\n55\t| 25 | MSVC PE (vs MinGW) | gap (MinGW seen D2) | `Rich`/`DanS` header, `.text$mn`, debug dir RSDS + `.pdb` path, `VCRUNTIME140.dll` | [I] `objdump -x f.exe`; python `pefile` (`RICH_HEADER`, `DIRECTORY_ENTRY_DEBUG`) | low-med |\n56\t| 26 | musl / static linking | seen D4, D5, D8, D12 (static); musl gap | no `.interp`, no `.dynamic`; musl: no `GLIBC_2.` version strings, `__libc_start_main` absent | [I] `readelf -lW f \\| grep -c INTERP`; `strings -a f \\| grep -c GLIBC_` | med (cheap twist \"Static\") |\n57\t| 27 | Mach-O thin / fat universal | gap (`lib.binary.macho_facts`) | `cffaedfe`/`cefaedfe` (thin), `cafebabe` + nfat_arch<20 (fat: collides with Java class magic), `__TEXT`/`__DATA_CONST`, `LC_MAIN` | [I] `/usr/lib/llvm-18/bin/llvm-otool -hlv f`; `llvm-lipo -info f`; `rz-bin -I f`; python `lief` | med-high (Swift/ObjC days were ELF, but `macho` already sits in the playbook format law; label presumed `macho`) |\n58\t| 28 | WebAssembly module | gap | `\\0asm\\x01\\0\\0\\0`, sections type/import/func/data; HCFG in a data segment | [M] `wasm-objdump -x f.wasm; wasm2wat f.wasm` (apt wabt); [I] rizin `rz-bin -I f.wasm`, Ghidra (no wasm loader by default) 