5, 5 sets / 800 ids on D16 (TT 30 s;\"\"\")\n# variant axes\nrep(\"\"\"  D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of\n  THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine).\"\"\",\"\"\"  D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of\n  THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine). Dispatch on MAGIC, not extension: `7f454c46` ELF, `MZ`\n  PE, `PK` jar, `\\\\0asm` + u32 version 1 WASM (D16: `wasm`/`wasm32`; `wasm64` only if a memory has limits flag 0x04 -- unconfirmed).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  digits...) is a `[^a-z0-9]+`-separated token of exactly one member name, answer `<field>` from THAT member only. Fallback if\n  names stop carrying the tag: stripped = the member without `.symtab`, symbolized/unstripped = the one with it. Config ids were\n  asked only for `stripped_` (same `.hcfg` in both).\"\"\",\"\"\"  digits...) is a `[^a-z0-9]+`-separated token of exactly one member name, answer `<field>` from THAT member only. Tags seen:\n  `stripped`/`symbolized` (D15), `compact`/`direct` (D16, two codegens of one wasm function: `select` chain vs nested\n  `if/else`, identical data section). Fallback if names stop carrying the tag: stripped = no `.symtab`; compact = the smaller\n  file / shorter code section. Config ids were asked only for ONE tag (D15 `stripped_`, D16 `compact_` -- both times the\n  alphabetically-first tag; the blob is identical in both members anyway). `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order, which was reverse-\n  alphabetical both days (symbolized, stripped; direct, compact): read the zip central directory, never sort names.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  BR15-004/003/002/001/000 -- set5 == the single's bytes); a carry-over\"\"\",\"\"\"  BR15-004/003/002/001/000 -- set5 == the single's bytes; D16: TT == the single's bytes BR16-000, Mastery BR16-001..005); a carry-over\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 (D8-D9), 3 (D10-D14), 5 (D15): loop\"\"\",\"\"\"  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 (D8-D9), 3 (D10-D14), 5 (D15-D16): loop\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal string literal in ELF `.rodata`, raw FPC `.data`): scan raw\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal string literal in ELF `.rodata`, raw FPC `.data`, RAW as the\n  first payload byte of WASM active data segment 0 (`i32.const 1024`; file 116/125), D16): scan raw\"\"\")\n# recognition cue\nrep(\"\"\"| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` |\"\"\",\"\"\"| `00 61 73 6d 01 00 00 00` (`\\\\0asm`), `.wasm`, ids `dNN_analysis_<tag>_format/architecture` (D16) | `lib.binary.wasm_layout(data)` (sections, memories, data_segments with file + memory offsets; handles 5-byte padded LEB128) or `wasm-objdump -x f.wasm` / `wasm2wat f.wasm` (wabt installed); format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32`. HCFG RAW in data segment 0 (`grep -abo HCFG`, crc-gate); segment 1 = a NUL-terminated `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1.sandboxed_module_inventory` marker (unasked). D16 module had NO import/table/elem section despite the \"imports, indirect calls\" prompt |\n| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` |\"\"\")\n# day by day\nold_d15=s[s.index(\"**D15 \\\"Stripped\\\"**\"):s.index(\"## GM answer conventions learned\")]\nnew_d=(\"\"\"**D15 \"Stripped\"** (150 Qs; 74 s, 0 wrong): stripped + symbolized C ELF pair, identical `.text`/`.hcfg`; only novelty = the\n`<qualifier>_` inside the field name (`_qualified(group, field)` router: file-name token -> member, `.symtab` fallback);\n`machine` `kind: integer` -> `62`; \"reconstruct calling conventions\" unasked. TT 5.2 s; Mastery 5 sets 9.35 s.\n\n**D16 \"Wasm Up\"** (internal slug `webassembly-optimization-equivalence`; 160 Qs; GM CORRECT 91 s after start, 0 wrong POSTs;\nTT + Mastery first try). Prompt: \"WebAssembly runs in a sandbox, but the sandbox has doors: imports, memory, indirect calls. Map\nevery door in this module and inventory what passes through.\" New group = TWO wasm MVP modules from one source:\n`d16--variant-000-compact.wasm` (561 B) and `-direct.wasm` (570 B). Sections type/function/memory(min 1)/export(`memory`,\n`evaluate`)/code/data, LLVM-style 5-byte padded LEB128 sizes; ONE function `evaluate(i32)->i32` mapping 0/1/2 to constants --\ncompact = `select` chain, direct = nested `if/else` (the \"optimization equivalence\"). NO import, table or element section.\nData seg 0 (mem 1024) = RAW HCFG (`01 c1` = ver 1, key 0xc1), seg 1 (mem 2048) = trace-marker string.\n- d16 ids: `sha256_1`/`_2` (archive order: direct, compact), `compact_`/`direct_` × format (`wasm`) + architecture (`wasm32`),\n  both `exact_text`; `compact_config_campaign/domain/mutex/url` only. No machine/hcfg_offset/import/export/table id.\n- How it went: race-harness POSTs banked the 150 old ids at T+25 s and the shas + configs at T+27 s (generic qualifier router +\n  raw HCFG scan already worked on wasm bytes); the worker added a 6-line `\\\\0asm` branch to the solver's container dispatch that\n  calls the prebuilt `lib.binary.wasm_layout` (format `wasm`, machine `wasm32`), and the 4 label ids went CORRECT on the\n  first try at T+91 s. The prebuild (`wasm-hcfg-data-segment`) paid for itself: no label guessing.\n- The sandbox \"doors\" theme (imports, memory, indirect calls) was NOT asked -- 12th day the theme is decoration -- but note the\n  module was built to have none of them; a later day may ask `imports`/`exports`/`memory_min`/`has_table` style ids.\n- TT correct, 64 s in-window of which download 52 s (bundle 32 MB; the solve was 7.6 s); Mastery 5 sets / 800 ids, 23 s in-window\n  (download 14.6 s, solve 2.9 s); Mastery set1 d01 STRIPPED again, set1 d02 a PE