{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZdzn9MGzypJAusfNrvbR6","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t  integer machine became pattern. Keep emitting the GM-confirmed spellings; the old REJECTED lists may be stale for pattern ids.\n41\t  (D14: `dNN_analysis_format` is still `exact_text` -> `elf`.)\n42\t\n43\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n44\t- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n45\t  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal string literal in ELF `.rodata`, raw FPC `.data`, RAW as the\n46\t  first payload byte of WASM active data segment 0 (`i32.const 1024`; file 116/125, D16)): scan raw\n47\t  bytes for `HCFG` and for `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (base64 of `HCFG`, std or urlsafe), decode, accept only if crc32(plain)\n48\t  matches AND the JSON parses -- keep scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw `HCFG` decoys); never a fixed offset.\n49\t  Storage did NOT change across a day's variants on any day so far (D14 `.hcfg` at file 0xfa0 in single/TT/all 3 sets).\n50\t- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9/D11-D13)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in\n51\t  the member: base64 form -> the `S` of `SENGR...` (D9 Nim 30696, D11 D 368272, D13 Crystal 560188 -- the text, not the String\n52\t  header 12 B before it); RAW form -> the `H` of `HCFG` (D12 FPC 82928). Constant across a day's variants although shas differ --\n53\t  still compute it: record `m.start()` of whichever scan hit (raw OR base64) validated, on BOTH paths (D12's raw path returned `none`).\n54\t- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (pure stdlib, ~15 ms / 2 MB, ~0.6 s / 67 MB).\n55\t  Returns every `HcfgHit` (offset, encoding, version, key, length, crc, crc_ok, config, plain, speculative, detail) best first;\n56\t  take `lib.binary.hcfg_find(data)` (first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit). Covers raw, base64 (std/url/wrapped), hex (plain, `48 43`,\n57\t  `48:43`, `\\x48`, `0x48, `), base32, base85, ascii85, UTF-16LE/BE of those, reversed raw/base64, single-byte xor'd base64/raw,\n58\t  zlib, gzip, raw deflate. Decoys come back `valid=False`. Offset convention per encoding (`hcfg_offset`):\n59\t\n60\t  | encoding | offset = | status |\n61\t  |---|---|---|\n62\t  | raw | the `H` of the magic | GM-confirmed (D12) |\n63\t  | base64 | first base64 char (`S` of `SENGR`) | GM-confirmed (D9/D11/D13) |\n64\t  | base64url, base32, base85, hex, hex-sep | first char of the stored text (`\\` of `\\x48`, `0` of `0x48`) | speculative |\n65\t  | ascii85 | the `<` of `<~` if present, else first char | speculative |\n66\t  | utf16le-* / utf16be-* | first byte of the first code unit (BE: its `00`); LE/BE tie -> the 2-aligned reading, else LE | speculative |\n67\t  | reversed-raw / reversed-base64 | lowest file offset of the reversed region | speculative |\n68\t  | xor-base64 / xor-raw | first stored byte (`detail` = `xor=0x..`) | speculative |\n69\t  | zlib / gzip / deflate | first byte of the compressed stream | speculative |\n70\t\n71\t  Wired into the binary solver as a fallback (kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0`); not needed on D14. A speculative offset is a\n72\t  first guess: if rejected, try the offset of the container header in front of the stored form next. Fixtures: `tests/data/hcfg_fixtures/`.\n73\t- **xor key / config values** -- re-roll per variant (`BRNN-00V`, `node-00V.dayNN...`, crc); derive from the header byte, never\n74\t  from the sample. D13 key = 0x91+N; D14 single BR14-000 key 0xa1, TT BR14-002, Mastery BR14-002/007/004.\n75\t- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member: Mastery set2 had d02 C++ as `.exe` (D3-D5, D7, D10) and d04\n76\t  Go as `.exe` (D4, D5, D7, D10); D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`)