e/elem; HCFG RAW at data seg 0 (mem 1024) | [I] `lib.binary.wasm_layout(data)`; `wasm-objdump -x f.wasm; wasm2wat f.wasm`; GM: format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32` (exact_text, first try) | high (carry-over; mastery may re-roll memory64 -> `wasm64`?) |\"\"\")\nrows_new = \"\"\"| 66 | Same-source build PAIR, qualifier ids `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` | seen D15 (stripped/symbolized), D16 (compact/direct) | two `dNN--variant-XXX-<tag>.<ext>` members, near-identical sizes, same HCFG; sha256_K = archive order (reverse-alpha both days); config asked for one tag only | [I] solver `_qualified` router (file-name token -> member; structural fallback) | high (2 days running; next tags: static/dynamic, O0/O2, pie/nopie, packed/unpacked, x86_64/aarch64) |\n| 67 | WASM \"doors\" inventory: imports, exports, memory limits, table/elem (`call_indirect`), start, globals, custom `name`/`producers` | gap (D16 prompt theme; unasked) | import section id 2 (`env.*`/`wasi_snapshot_preview1.*`), table id 4, elem id 9, `call_indirect` 0x11 | [I] `wasm-objdump -x -j Import -j Export -j Table -j Elem f`; extend `lib.binary.wasm_layout` | med-high (theme ids could land with tomorrow's carry-over backfill) |\n| 68 | WASM from real toolchains (Emscripten, wasi-sdk/clang, Rust, Go, AssemblyScript), memory64, passive segments, HCFG in custom section / split / i32.store-built | gap | `global.get __memory_base` init expr, `memory.init` 0xfc 08, `producers` section, AssemblyScript UTF-16 strings, Go `go:buildid` | [I] `wasm2wat`, `wasm-decompile`; `hcfg_scan` (utf16) ; clang-18 `--target=wasm32-wasi -c` (object only: no wasm-ld) | med |\n| 69 | eBPF object (ELF e_machine 247) | gap | ELF64 ET_REL, sections `license`, `.maps`, `xdp`/`kprobe/...`/`tracepoint/...`, `.BTF`/`.BTF.ext` | [I] `readelf -hSW f.o` (machine \"Linux BPF\"); `llvm-objdump-18 -d f.o`; `clang-18 -target bpf -c` builds fixtures | med (natural \"sandboxed code\" sequel to WASM) |\n| 70 | Bytecode containers: LLVM bitcode, Python `.pyc`, Lua `luac`, standalone `.class`/`.dex` | gap | `BC\\\\xc0\\\\xde` / wrapper `de c0 17 0b`; pyc magic `xx 0d 0d 0a`; `\\\\x1bLua`; `CAFEBABE` major>=45; `dex\\\\n035` | [I] `llvm-dis-18`/`llvm-bcanalyzer-18`; `pycdas`; `luac -l -l`; `javap`; jadx | low-med (format label unknown -> submit alone) |\n| 71 | Section-less / corrupted ELF headers (sstrip, e_shnum 0, bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx) | gap | `readelf -S`: \"There are no sections\", pyelftools exceptions, PT_LOAD only | [I] `readelf -lW f`; parse program headers; `rz-bin -I f`; HCFG via raw scan | med (next escalation of \"Stripped\") |\n\"\"\"\nanchor = \"\\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\"\ni = s.index(anchor)\ns = s[:i].rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + rows_new + s[i:]\n# recognition cues\nrep(\"\"\"  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 00617373 \\\\0asm => WASM ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n  0061736d \\\\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32` (GM-confirmed); lib.binary.wasm_layout -> sections, memories,\n    data_segments (file_offset + mem_offset); wasm-objdump -x F ; HCFG RAW in data seg 0 -> raw scan finds it (crc-gate)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\"\"\")\n# readiness gaps\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=s.index(\"```json\",i)+len(\"```json\"); k=s.index(\"```\",j)\ngaps=json.loads(s[j:k])\ndrop={\"wabt\",\"floss\",\"wasm-hcfg-data-segment\",\"imports-buildid-fields\"}\nbuilt={\"upx-packed-hcfg\",\"aes-tea-chacha-hcfg\",\"stack-built-hcfg\",\"multiarch-machine-labels\",\"macho-hcfg-section\",\"resource-overlay-hcfg\",\"rolling-xor-hcfg\",\"init-time-decoder\",\"shared-object-relocatable\",\"exotic-codecs\"}\nold={g[\"id\"]:g for g in gaps}\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"build-pair-router\",\"concept\":\"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs dynamic, -pie vs -no-pie, -g vs stripped, upx'd vs plain, each with a `.hcfg` section and file-name tags. Target: router matches the LONGEST tag token of exactly one member name; structural fallback per tag family (no INTERP = static, ET_DYN+INTERP = pie, UPX! = packed, .debug_info = debug, smaller code = compact/optimized); per-member fields that DIFFER inside a pair (elf_type, entry_point, has_symtab, section_names, imports) answered from that member; sha256_K from zip central-directory order.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cross-arch-pair\",\"concept\":\"Same source built for x86-64 + AArch64 (+ RISC-V/ARM .o) as a pair, arch-named qualifiers\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15 links, clang-18 --target=riscv64/armv7 -c gives ET_REL. Name tags like `-x86_64.elf`/`-aarch64.elf`/`-arm64` put an UNDERSCORE inside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_64_machine`): the router must try multi-token tags before splitting at the first `_`. Expected labels from multiarch-machine-labels (x86-64, AArch64, RISC-V, ARM; kind:integer 62/183/243/40); HCFG ints stay LE on these arches.\"},\n {\"id\":\"wasm-inventory-fields\",\"concept\":\"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add them. Build fixtures with wat2wasm (installed): imports from env/wasi_snapshot_preview1 (func/memory/table/global), funcref table + active elem, call_indirect, start, mutable globals, passive segment, name + producers custom sections. Extend lib.binary.wasm_layout with imports [{module,name,kind}], exports [{name,kind,index}], tables, elems, start, globals, custom_names; candidate spellings: JSON list of `module.name` in section order, counts as integers, memory_min in pages, has_table true/false, hcfg_offset = file offset of the `H` (record mem_offset too).\"},\n {\"id\":\"wasm-hcfg-hidden\",\"concept\":\"WASM HCFG not a plain active data segment: custom section `hcfg`, passive segment + memory.init, split across segments, built by i32.store immediates, UTF-16 (AssemblyScript), memory64 module\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Natural Mastery/next-day twist of D16. Fixtures via wat2wasm: (a) custom section named hcfg (has_hcfg_section analogue -> `true`), (b) passive segment, (c) blob split over two active segments at adjacent mem offsets (reassemble linear memory image then hcfg_find), (d) code-built: run of `i32.const addr; i32.const imm; i32.store` -> collect imms in order (or a tiny stack interpreter over the function body), (e) memory64 limits flag 0x04 -> machine `wasm64` speculative. Never execute the module (no wasmtime).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ebpf-object\",\"concept\":\"eBPF ELF object (e_machine 247) with HCFG in .rodata / a map section\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"clang-18 -target bpf -O2 -c fixture with SEC(\\\"xdp\\\"), a `license` section, `.maps`, and an HCFG `.hcfg`/`.rodata` blob. Targets: format `elf`, elf_type ET_REL, machine readelf spelling `Linux BPF` (EM_BPF; integer 247), entry_point 0x0, has_hcfg_section; program section names as a possible `programs` field. Plausible next 'sandboxed code' after WASM.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bytecode-containers\",\"concept\":\"LLVM bitcode, Python .pyc, Lua luac, standalone .class/.dex as group members\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Fixtures: clang-18 -c -emit-llvm (BC C0 DE + wrapper), python -m py_compile (3.x magic), luac (installed), javac single class. Record magic -> candidate format labels (`llvm_bitcode`/`bitcode`, `pyc`, `luac`/`lua`, `class`, `dex`) and architecture (`none`?); HCFG as a string constant (raw or base64) -> hcfg_scan; submit any new label alone.\"},\n {\"id\":\"sstrip-corrupt-headers\",\"concept\":\"ELF without section headers (sstrip, e_shnum=0) or with bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx/fake section names\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets: parser never crashes (pyelftools wrapped, header fields from raw struct), section_names `[]`, has_symtab false, has_hcfg_section false unless the literal name exists, HCFG via raw scan; entry_point/machine still from the ELF header.\"},\n {\"id\":\"provenance-facts-extractor\",\"concept\":\"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as int and ISO. Fixtures from the existing TARGETS.json builds (gcc -g, -Wl,--build-id). Spellings unknown -> submit alone.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-imports-exports-facts\",\"concept\":\"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions (`dll!func`?), exports, imphash; Mach-O LC_LOAD_DYLIB. JSON compact like symbols. D15 symbolized had getenv/strcmp/printf, unasked.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-singlefile-aot\",\"concept\":\".NET single-file bundle, ReadyToRun and NativeAOT builds\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"dotnet installed: `dotnet publish -p:PublishSingleFile=true` (apphost + bundle manifest, `.net core bundle` signature hash), `-p:PublishReadyToRun=true` (R2R header in CLI dll), `-p:PublishAot=true` (native ELF, no BSJB). Targets: format label shift (pe_cli vs elf), HCFG location inside the bundle (embedded dll offset) -> hcfg_scan on the bundle bytes.\"},\n]\nkeep=[g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"] not in drop]\n# demote built prebuilds out of the queue order (keep for history at the end)\nout=[g for g in new]\nfor g in keep:\n    if g[\"id\"] in built: continue\n    out.append(g)\nout_built=[g for g in keep if g[\"id\"] in built]\nfor g in out_built: g[\"priority\"]=3\n# tweak existing notes/tools\nfor g in out:\n    if g[\"id\"]==\"erlang-lua-decompilers\":\n        g[\"detail\"]=\"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"\n    if g[\"id\"]==\"qemu-user-static\": g[\"priority\"]=2\n    if g[\"id\"]==\"checksec-fields\": g[\"priority\"]=2\nids=[g[\"id\"] for g in out+out_built]\nassert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nfinal=sorted(out,key=lambda g:g[\"priority\"])+out_built\ntxt=\"\\n\"+\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps({k:g[k] for k in (\"id\",\"concept\",\"priority\",\"action\",\"detail\")},ensure_ascii=False) for g in final)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:j]+txt+s[k:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(len(final), [ (g['id'],g['priority'],g['action']) for g in final]