and more non-ELF containers (Mach-O, eBPF, bytecode). Asked field names are a small\nfixed pool (config_*, format, machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names,\ndisassembly, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, xor_key_hex, metadata_version,\ncompression_methods); the prompt's language theme has not been asked since D4. So for D17+ the biggest risks are (a) a twist that\nhides the HCFG from a byte scan (packing, real crypto, stack-built), (b) a new container/arch whose LABEL we have never spelled\n(Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64, MIPS...), (c) a new field family (imports/exports, memory/table \"doors\" -- the D16 prompt's theme --,\nbuild-id, protections), (d) a pair qualifier that itself contains `_` (`x86_64_machine`) breaking a split-at-first-`_` router.\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\nMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\nunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n\n35:| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 (+ every day's d01)  | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] \n61:| 27 | Mach-O thin / fat universal | prebuilt (macho-hcfg-section; never seen)  | `cffaedfe`/`cefaedfe` (thin), `cafebabe` + nfat_arch<20\n62:| 28 | WebAssembly module | **seen D16** (`-compact`/`-direct` pair) | `\\0asm` + u32 1, 5-byte padded LEB128 sizes; D16: type/function/me\n63:| 29 | Relocatable object (ELF ET_REL / COFF .o) | prebuilt (shared-object-relocatable)  | ELF e_type 1, `.rela.text`, no program headers\n64:| 30 | Shared library (.so ET_DYN / .dll) | prebuilt (shared-object-relocatable)  | `ET_DYN` with no `.interp`, SONAME, exported dynsyms;\n67:| 33 | AArch64 | prebuilt label (multiarch-machine-labels), never seen  | e_machine 183 (0xb7); PE 0xaa64; Mach-O cputype 0x0100000c | [I\n71:| 37 | UPX packed | prebuilt (upx-packed-hcfg)  | `UPX!` in first 4 KB, sections `UPX0`/`UPX1`, entropy > 7.2, tiny section table | [I] `\n73:| 39 | Stripped (no `.symtab`) | seen D15 (+ D8/D15/D16 Mastery d01)  | `readelf -S` lacks `.symtab`/`.strtab`; `file` says \"stripped\" | \n87:| 53 | Block/stream ciphers: AES (ECB/CBC/CTR/GCM), XTEA/TEA, ChaCha20/Salsa20 | prebuilt (aes-tea-chacha-hcfg)  | AES S-box `63 7c 77 7b\n88:| 54 | Rolling / index xor (`k+i`, `k^prev`, xor with `crc`/len) | prebuilt (rolling-xor-hcfg)  | short decode loop `xor byte [rdi+rax], \n89:| 55 | Stack-built / code-built blob (mov imm to stack, per-char pushes) | prebuilt (stack-built-hcfg; floss installed)  | runs of `mov d\n90:| 56 | Resources: PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class file, Mach-O section | prebuilt (resource-overlay-hcfg)  | `.rsrc` \n91:| 57 | Overlay (bytes after last section / appended) | prebuilt (resource-overlay-hcfg)  | file s